issues.description:
## Context

`fhe-factory.ts` has `MAX_TENANT_SERVICES=100` limit on the `tenantServiceInstances` map with `evictLRUTenant()`. However, the current implementation is FIFO (first-in, first-out) by insertion order — it evicts the oldest entry regardless of access order.

A true LRU (Least Recently Used) cache should evict the **least recently accessed** entry when capacity is reached.

## Current Behavior

`evictLRUTenant()` calls `tenantServiceInstances.keys().next().value` which returns the **oldest** entry by insertion order. Accessing an entry with `.get()` does not update its position.

## Expected Behavior

When `storeTenantService()` is called and `tenantServiceInstances.size >= MAX_TENANT_SERVICES`, evict the **least recently accessed** entry, not the oldest by insertion time.

## Implementation Options

### Option A: LinkedHashMap-style manual tracking (Recommended — simplest, no external deps)

Maintain a parallel `Map<string, number>` for access order timestamps. On every `.get()` and `.set()`, update the timestamp. On eviction, find and remove the entry with the oldest timestamp.

```typescript
// In fhe-factory.ts
private tenantAccessOrder = new Map<string, number>();

private evictLRUTenant(): void {
  let oldestKey: string | null = null;
  let oldestTime = Infinity;
  for (const [key, time] of this.tenantAccessOrder) {
    if (time < oldestTime) {
      oldestTime = time;
      oldestKey = key;
    }
  }
  if (oldestKey) {
    this.tenantServiceInstances.delete(oldestKey);
    this.tenantAccessOrder.delete(oldestKey);
  }
}
```

Update `storeTenantService()` to call `tenantAccessOrder.set(tenantId, Date.now())` after insert. Update `getTenantFHEService()` to call `tenantAccessOrder.set(tenantId, Date.now())` after access.

### Option B: Use a proper LRU library

Consider `lru-cache` npm package. Adds a dependency but battle-tested.

### Option C: Use a WeakMap with manual tracking

Overkill for this use case.

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] `evictLRUTenant()` evicts the least recently accessed entry, not the oldest by insertion order
- [ ] Calling `getTenantFHEService(tenantId)` updates its access time so it won't be evicted immediately after
- [ ] Existing tests pass
- [ ] Add unit test verifying LRU behavior: access A, B, C, then access A, then evict — verify C is evicted, not A or B
